      "content": "The feeling that the damage is irreversible is a symptom of deep distress, not necessarily reality. Self-worth is not based on the mistakes we make, but on our capacity to learn and grow from them. Even when actions feel permanent, perspective and behavior can shift, which is where true change begins. Please allow someone, like a therapist, to help you unpack these rigid beliefs about your identity.",
      "source": "target",
